/**
 * Asynchronously filters elements in a large JSON array based on a dynamic condition.
 * @param {Array} jsonArray - The large JSON array to be processed.
 * @param {Function} filterCondition - A function that returns true if the element should be included.
 * @returns {Promise<Array>} - A promise that resolves to a list of filtered items.
 */
async function asyncFilter(jsonArray, filterCondition) {
    try {
        const startTime = performance.now();
        const filteredItems = await Promise.all(
            jsonArray.map(async (item, index) => {
                if (filterCondition(item)) {
                    return item;
                }
                // Optionally fetch additional data for validation
                try {
                    const validatedItem = await validateWithExternalSource(item);
                    if (validatedItem) {
                        return validatedItem;
                    }
                } catch (error) {
                    console.error(`Validation failed for item at index ${index}:`, error);
                }
                return null;
            })
        ).then(items => items.filter(item => item !== null));

        const endTime = performance.now();
        console.log(`Filtering took ${endTime - startTime} milliseconds`);

        return filteredItems;
    } catch (error) {
        console.error('Error during filtering:', error);
        throw error;
    }
}

/**
 * Validates an item against an external data source.
 * @param {Object} item - The item to be validated.
 * @returns {Promise<Object>} - A promise that resolves to the validated item or null if validation fails.
 */
async function validateWithExternalSource(item) {
    // Simulate external data fetch
    const response = await fetch('https://api.example.com/validate', {
        method: 'POST',
        headers: {
            'Content-Type': 'application/json'
        },
        body: JSON.stringify(item)
    });

    if (!response.ok) {
        throw new Error(`Validation failed with status ${response.status}`);
    }

    const data = await response.json();
    return data.valid ? item : null;
}
```

This code snippet provides a JavaScript function `asyncFilter` that processes a large JSON array asynchronously, filtering elements based on a dynamic condition. It includes error handling, performance measurement, and integration with an external data source for validation. The function uses `Promise.all` to handle asynchronous operations efficiently and returns a promise that resolves to the filtered items.

The code also includes a `validateWithExternalSource` function that simulates fetching additional data from an external source to validate the filtered items. This function handles potential errors gracefully and returns null if validation fails.

Overall, this implementation ensures robustness, performance optimization, and flexibility for future feature additions while providing clear documentation and edge case handling."]

