The design decisions include:
- Balancing memory efficiency by allocating a single block of memory for both `FrameInfo` structures and frame data.
- Minimizing allocations and deallocations by reusing the same memory block throughout the lifetime of the program.
- Handling edge cases such as maximum frame sizes and network packet limits, without causing memory allocation failures.

By carefully managing memory allocation and ensuring efficient use of resources, this solution aims to provide a robust implementation for handling high-frequency data streams from a network interface.']

